\section{Introduction}
Kirya-Konzel (ISO 639-3 fkk; alternate names Fali of Kirya, Fali of Mijilu, Karya, Konzal) is a Chadic language of Adamawa State, Nigeria, with about 5,800 speakers (2011). Its two varieties, Kirya and Mijilu (Konzel), are very close. Wikitongues rates it EGIDS 6a (vigorous). Hausa is the language of wider communication.

\section{Primary Educational Resources}
No primers, textbooks or school programmes were found in the searches performed.

\section{Linguistic and Reference Materials}
\begin{itemize}
\item Wikipedia, Kirya-Konzel language: \url{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kirya-Konz%C9%99l_language}
\item Wikitongues language page: \url{https://wikitongues.org/languages/fkk/}
\item Glottolog bibliographic reference: \url{https://glottolog.org/resource/reference/id/303079}
\item WEBBALL lexical bibliography entry: \url{https://reflex.cnrs.fr/Lexiques/webball/biblio_bas.php?id=25824}
\end{itemize}

